# The compiler's types, each kind a struct (#593). Inference reads a type
# off every expression, and pinning, lowering, and the emitter work with
# what it reads. A type was a tagged array, `["maybe", ["integer"]]`: a
# String beside an array, nested to any depth, which a native array cannot
# be. Each kind moves here as it becomes a struct, and is written by its
# fields' names.
#
# A file of its own, required ahead of everything that names a type, since
# a file runs its constants before it declares its structs, and the
# compiler's constants are full of types.

# A maybe of a type (ADR 0040 §3): the wrapper, never a union, holding the
# type of the value where it is there.
struct MaybeType
  inner
end
